Every note switch triggered a full `loadHTMLString` reload — revalidating the MathJax CDN, re-parsing megabytes of JS, and reinitializing the math engine. Regex patterns were also reconstructed on every `parseToHTML` call.

## SPA Architecture + Persistent MathJax (`ReadingView.swift`)

`WebViewPool` now loads a persistent shell HTML (CSS + MathJax + nevado.js, empty `<body>`) once per WebView lifetime. Note switches update only the DOM body via JavaScript — no page reload, no MathJax reinitialization:

```swift
// Before: full reload on every note change
nsView.loadHTMLString(html, baseURL: Bundle.main.resourceURL)

// After: body-only injection, MathJax persists
webView.evaluateJavaScript("""
(function() {
    window.onyxImageSizeMode = \(sizeModeJson);
    window.onyxImageSizeValue = \(sizeValue);
    document.body.innerHTML = \(jsonString);
    window.scrollTo(0, 0);
    if (window.MathJax) {
        if (window.MathJax.typesetClear) { MathJax.typesetClear([document.body]); }
        if (window.MathJax.typesetPromise) { MathJax.typesetPromise([document.body]); }
    }
})();
""")
```

`Coordinator` gains `isShellLoaded` to gate injection. Content arriving before the shell finishes loading is buffered in `pendingBodyHTML` and flushed in `webView(_:didFinish:)`, which now fires exactly once.

`sizeMode` and `bodyHTML` are serialized via `JSONEncoder` before embedding into JS to prevent injection.

## Static Regex Compilation (`MarkdownParser.swift`)

14 `RegexBuilder` patterns previously allocated on every `parseToHTML` call are promoted to `private static let` properties — automata built once per app lifecycle:

```swift
// Before: new Regex instance (and deferred compilation) on every call
let boldAstRegex = Regex { "**"; Capture { ... }; "**" }

// After: compiled once, reused across all parses
private static let boldAstRegex = Regex { "**"; Capture { ... }; "**" }
```

Also fixes 13 redundant `trimmingCharacters(in: .whitespaces)` calls per line in the paragraph-wrapping loop (already had `trimmed` but conditions re-computed it from `line`).

Adds `makeShellHTML()` — a public static helper wrapping `wrapInHTML(content: "")` — used by `WebViewPool` to generate the persistent shell.

