All 5 password hash comparisons in `server/server.js` used `===`/`!==`, which are vulnerable to timing side-channel attacks.

Replaced with a `timingSafeCompare` helper using `crypto.timingSafeEqual`:

```js
function timingSafeCompare(a, b) {
  const bufA = Buffer.from(String(a));
  const bufB = Buffer.from(String(b));
  try {
    return crypto.timingSafeEqual(bufA, bufB);
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}
```

