The project's 14 unit-test executables used a hand-rolled harness (`check()`/`Fail()`/`Pass()` + `std::exit()`) with one `main()` per binary — no framework, no per-test granularity, abort-on-first-failure semantics.

## Changes

### Dependencies
- `CMakeLists.txt`: `find_package(GTest QUIET)` with FetchContent v1.14.0 fallback inside `if(BUILD_TESTING)`; `include(GoogleTest)` for `gtest_discover_tests()`.

### `navigation_test_harness.hh`
- Dropped `Fail()` / `Pass()` / `std::exit()`.
- Base helpers (`ExpectNear`, `ExpectVectorNear`, `ExpectInsideClassification`, `ExpectTrue`) now delegate to `EXPECT_NEAR` / `EXPECT_LE` / `EXPECT_EQ` / `EXPECT_TRUE` — non-fatal, accumulates all failures per test.
- Domain helpers (`ExpectInside`, `ExpectSurfaceNormal`, `ExpectDistanceToIn/Out`, …) and fixture structs (`BoxFixture`, `SphereFixture`, `CylinderFixture`) are unchanged.

### All 14 unit test `.cc` files
Removed `check()` helper and `main()`. Test functions are now `TEST(Suite, Case)` bodies:

```cpp
// Before
static void test_box_solid() {
  check(solid.GetName() == "TestBox", "solid name is 'TestBox'");
  ...
}
int main() { test_box_solid(); ... }

// After
TEST(SolidBasicAPI, BoxSolid) {
  EXPECT_EQ(solid.GetName(), "TestBox");
  ...
}
